                "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 1 at 7:07PM MST until September 1 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "description": "FFWPSR\n\nThe National Weather Service in Phoenix has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWestern Yuma County in southwestern Arizona...\nSouthwestern La Paz County in west central Arizona...\nSoutheastern Imperial County in southeastern California...\n\n* Until 1000 PM MST /1000 PM PDT/.\n\n* At 707 PM MST /707 PM PDT/, local law enforcement reported\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between\n1 and 1.75 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts\nup to 0.5 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...California Highway Patrol reported flooding along I-8 near\nOgilby Rd.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Western Yuma, Southwestern La Paz and\nSoutheastern Imperial Counties.\n\nThis includes CA Interstate 8 between mile markers 83 and 92.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nMarcus Wash, Colorado River, Picacho Wash, Unnamed Wash, Little\nPicacho Wash, Mission Wash, Ferguson Wash, Senator Wash, Carrizo\nWash and Araz Wash.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
